 - **Minimum Stack size before war**: Added a minimum stack unit count requirement to prevent the stack from being marked as "ready" until it has enough units: no `MOVE_DECLARE_WAR` flag, no premature advance toward the city, and AI keeps building units until the stack is big enough. Helps fix the **issue of "back and forth" war declarations with immediate retreat without city attack**: low-numbered unit stacks were especially sensible to power swings (city defenses, one more enemy units skews win chance, etc.). Change in `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`. See [KI#104](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#104---tremendously-improved-base-advciv-issue-of-the-weird-back-and-forth-of-declaring-war-moving-a-stack-then-withdrawing-without-attacking-which-is-extremely-inefficient).
 - **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but).
 - **Early-game razing — distance-aware captures**: Updated conquer/raze logic so that, for roughly the first **~120 turns** (scaled by game speed), the AI **razes captured cities** that aren’t **close enough** to justify early investment, in `CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity`. This addresses the base AdvCiv pattern where forces overextend (most troops sit in a faraway capture while **core cities** thin out) and also preserves scarce early economy (city maintenance, low pop, time to build improvements/culture). Indirect effect: less fog-busting far from us → **more barbarians** there, which tends to pressure rivals. Net: a **stronger, more focused** early AI (fewer "split in two" empires). See [KI#64](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity).

